<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: EU set to agree stability pact by mid-Dec - Santer.</title>
<headline>EU set to agree stability pact by mid-Dec - Santer.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Commission President Jacques Santer expects the European Union to have reached agreement on a budget stability pact by the EU's summit in Dublin on December 13 and 14, according to a speech read on his behalf on Monday.</p>
<p>The speech, written by Santer, said he also expected agreement on a successor to the Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM) to be reached at the Dublin summit.</p>
<p>Santer was due to give the speech at the European Finance Convention in Dublin, but could not travel to Dublin because of ill health, organisers said.  </p>
<p>His speech was read on his behalf by Colm Larkin, the director of the EC representation in Ireland.</p>
